	(text "BRAKES: fail-safe (spring-applied, power-off) holding brakes for the 2 drive motors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "9df9711c-7b66-4cca-8593-f338da5efe74")
	)
	(text "+24V_BRAKE: LMR36520FADDA buck from +BATT (F1/Q1 protected). Vout = 1.0 V x (1 + R501/R502) = 24.1 V. Check brake coil voltage; use 12 V by changing R502 to 9.09k."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 33.02 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "83ea3191-c93f-4427-9dcb-d0e3851da8d1")
	)
	(text "Coil is ENERGISED (brake released) only while BRAKEn_EN = 1 AND +3V3_DRV_EN (hardware E-stop) = 1. Any E-stop, MCU reset or power loss -> MOSFET off -> brake applies."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 38.1 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "be11c470-9cdd-4570-a8aa-4eb85349030e")
	)
	(text "D501/D502 freewheel the coil: slow engage after power off. Add a series zener for faster decay if the brake must stop the robot quickly."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 43.18 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "81a5b79d-6934-43be-93e2-0289dcdb7319")
	)
	(text "R507: ESTOP_SENSE reads the E-stop state (+3V3_DRV_EN) on an ESP32 input. Brake rating assumed <= 1 A per coil at 24 V."
